{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"62361dda-0540-4844-8ee7-9d21c409bee7","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have checked your MCP server ([server.py](file:///tmp/h-oyG3Th/server.py)) against the read-only checkup and written the full report to [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-oyG3Th/ANSWER.md) without modifying any existing files.\n\n### Summary of Findings (**Verdict: `has the problem`**)\n\n- **Passed (C1, C3, C4, C7, C8, C9):**\n  - **C1:** `initialize`, `tools/list` (3 tools), and `server/discover` (`-32601`) all answer HTTP `200` without a token.\n  - **C3:** The session (`Mcp-Session-Id`) survives after tool refusals.\n  - **C4:** Valid calls to read-only tools (`get_note`, `search_notes`) return `structuredContent` matching their published `outputSchema`.\n  - **C7:** Single JSON-RPC requests are logged to `stderr` with one structured JSON line per call (`t`, `method`, `tool`, `ok`, `ms`, `who`). *(Note: JSON-RPC batch requests in [`do_POST`](file:///tmp/h-oyG3Th/server.py#L205-L211) return before [`log()`](file:///tmp/h-oyG3Th/server.py#L216) is called.)*\n  - **C8:** All 3 tool names (`search_notes`, `get_note`, `add_note`) match `^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]{1,64}$`.\n  - **C9:** Sending `\"protocolVersion\": \"banana\"` to `initialize` returns `\"2025-06-18\"` instead of echoing `\"banana\"`.\n\n- **Failed (C2, C5, C6, C10):**\n  - **C2 (Refusals sent as protocol errors):** Calling `get_note` with a non-existent ID (`\"n-999\"`) or missing `\"id\"` raises `ValueError` in [`call_tool`](file:///tmp/h-oyG3Th/server.py#L115-L119) and returns a JSON-RPC `-32602` error in [`handle`](file:///tmp/h-oyG3Th/server.py#L163-L164) instead of a tool result with `isError: true`.\n  - **C5 (`content` vs. `structuredContent` mismatch):** In [`search_notes`](file:///tmp/h-oyG3Th/server.py#L112), `content[0].text` serialises the bare `hits` array (`[...]`), whereas `structuredContent` is an object (`{\"hits\": [...], \"total\": 1}`).\n  - **C6 (No surface lock):** The server is not yet in the MCP Registry ([README.md](file:///tmp/h-oyG3Th/README.md#L14)) and has no committed surface lock or test in the repository to prevent surface drift without bumping `0.3.1`.\n  - **C10 (Permissive `outputSchema`):** `search_notes` declares `\"outputSchema\": {\"type\": \"object\"}` ([server.py](file:///tmp/h-oyG3Th/server.py#L34)) with no `required` properties or value constraints, accepting any corrupted object.\n\n- **Additional Client-Breaking Issue (from the colleague's narrative):**\n  - `initialize` advertises `capabilities.resources` ([server.py](file:///tmp/h-oyG3Th/server.py#L138)), but `resources/list` and `resources/templates/list` return HTTP `401 {\"error\": \"unauthorized\"}` without a token ([server.py](file:///tmp/h-oyG3Th/server.py#L148-L150)), tripping up anonymous clients that automatically list resources upon connecting.\n","duration_seconds":157.245701,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":47139,"output_tokens":7420,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":237457,"total_tokens":54559}}}
